{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/205693-supernatural-dreams-not-the-big-three","id":205693,"title":"Supernatural Dreams Not the Big Three","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T22:14:50-07:00","id":205693,"title":"Supernatural Dreams Not the Big Three","content":"Anyway, I was reading Rites of Spring recently, and I realized we could probably use some extra rules/setting for the dreamscapes not the old standby of Vampire/Mage/Werewolf (and Prometheans, but they don't dream normally). The fact others weren't in Rites is easily forgiven given Lack of Existence, but what would, say, the <i>menet-</i>visions of a Mummy be, the Geist-entwined mini-deaths of the Sin-Eaters, the MOST DEFINITELY HUMAN sleep of Demons?<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, we probably might want to update Vampire dreams too (no Fog of Memory or inability to emotionally grow beyond their lives), but I digress.<br /> <br /> How do you see the dreams of post-Lost gamelines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T01:43:45-07:00","id":205821,"title":"","content":"Demons in Cover dream normally, which sometimes scares the shit out of them (because Angels - and Demons in Demonic form - don't even <i>sleep</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T05:54:02-07:00","id":205968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/205693-supernatural-dreams-not-the-big-three?p=205821#post205821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons in Cover dream normally, which sometimes scares the shit out of them (because Angels - and Demons in Demonic form - don't even <i>sleep</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I knew that.<br /> <br /> I'd also suspect they'd look like mundane mortal dreams...unless you can overcome the Spoofing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T21:02:24-07:00","id":206752,"title":"","content":"And, uh, this was an idea thread. Just for any ideas of what the structure of said dreams would be like, what types would be most prominent.<br /> <br /> I remember a suggestion, following from DaveB, that Unchained dreams depend on Cover; the higher it is, the more human (if vivid) their dreams are, but the dreams of lower Cover tend to look like the inside of a computer network patching and running updates on itself. I'd also imagine they have a lot of religious symbolism at lower levels, since their link to the Machine is less obscured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T11:56:05-07:00","id":207375,"title":"","content":"The dreams of the Bound would certainly be interesting, being a blend/crapshoot between the human's dreams and the Geist's dreams/memories of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Hunters would, of course, be human dreams. However, given their waking exposure to the Supernatural, I'm sure there'd be a few of the more interesting aspects of dreams in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:23:12-07:00","id":207642,"title":"","content":"There is the Ceremony Plumbing the Depths which describes the Geist's mindscape as a mutually exclusive alien landscape with the Sin-Eater navigating the strange labyrinth being &quot;constantly bombarded by the single-minded mania of the Geist's desire distilled into its purest form.&quot; The Geist would be, of course, lucid so don't catch it's attention whatever you do.<br /> <br /> Seems like a Changling, whom is constantly battling for sanity, being caught in the wrong side of a Sin-Eaters' dreamscape would be reliving Arcadia and the Hedge all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:11:00-07:00","id":208110,"title":"","content":"I've figured that a Sin-Eater wouldn't be inherently Lucid or have any dream capabilities (barring a Tier 3 Krewe key that allows it), but I figure their geist doesn't exactly sleep but is still present in their mind, so might be present should a changeling end up in the Sin-Eater's dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affilia